{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And the servants of Isaac came and told him about the well which they had dug.</b> This is what is stated above (Genesis 26:25), \"And the servants of Isaac dug there a well,\" for they had begun to dig it when Abimelech came to him in those days, and on the day of the covenant, when they departed from him, they announced to him that they had found water. And it seems likely to me that it is the well that Abraham dug and for which he gave seven ewe-lambs as a testimony (Genesis 21:30), for the Philistines had stopped it up along with the others, and Isaac returned and dug it, and he called it by the same name that his father had called it. Therefore the name of the city is Be'er Sheva, after the name of the well which both father and son called by that name, for there they both swore. And this well alludes to the Tabernacle of Shiloh, and the Philistines stopped it up when the Ark was taken (I Samuel 4:11), and he returned and they dug it, for so they returned the Ark with the offering to Elohim (ibid. 6:11)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:35:38.134807549Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}